when I can get outof memory error in case of arraylist in java													
>> If the array is very large, the JVM may not have enough contiguous memory available.													
https://dip-mazumder.medium.com/java-memory-leaks-a-comprehensive-guide-to-causes-and-solutions-17e319523499#:~:text=This%20is%20because%20the%20Java,to%20throw%20an%20OutOfMemoryError%20exception.													
													
In Java, an OutOfMemoryError can occur with ArrayList in a few scenarios:													
"Large Data Sets: If you're trying to store a massive amount of data in an
 ArrayList and your system doesn't have enough memory to accommodate it,
 you might encounter an OutOfMemoryError. 
This is more likely to happen when dealing with very large datasets or when the available heap memory is limited."													
													
"Memory Leaks: If your code has memory leaks, where objects are being 
held in memory unnecessarily and not released for garbage collection,
 it can eventually lead to running out of memory. For instance, 
if you keep adding objects to an ArrayList without ever removing them when 
they're no longer needed, memory usage can keep increasing until it exceeds available resources."													
													
"Inefficient Memory Usage: Sometimes, inefficient use of memory can lead to OutOfMemoryError.
 For instance, if you're storing large objects in an ArrayList, each object consumes memory. If the objects are large and the list grows too big, it can exceed available memory."													
													
To mitigate OutOfMemoryError with ArrayList, you can:													
													
Use a smaller dataset if possible.													
Optimize your code to use memory more efficiently.													
Ensure that you're removing objects from the ArrayList when they're no longer needed.													
Increase the heap size of your Java Virtual Machine (JVM) if feasible, although this might not be a sustainable solution for large-scale applications.													
													
